      <workList xml:id="workDesc_fe415b35">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e234231">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_e3df2816">B2:017</identifier>
            <title xml:id="_19" xml:lang="de">Cantata auf das heilige Oster-Fest</title>
            <title type="alternative" xml:id="title_ebb07228" xml:lang="de">Der Herr wird zu uns kommen</title>
            <title type="subordinate" xml:id="title_ea320832" xml:lang="de">In Festo Paschatos. Feria II</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_2923c098">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="_21">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_22_0">
               <eventList type="performances" xml:id="eventList_bf2bc416">
                  <event xml:id="event_8749cde0">
                     <date isodate="1770" xml:id="date_7c3860b9">Easter 1770</date>
                     <geogName role="place" xml:id="geogName_852bb40c">Zurich</geogName>
                     <biblList xml:id="biblList_2e6cd3be">
                        <head xml:id="head_c6bccb9a">Reviews</head>
                        <bibl label="" xml:id="bibl_bfa05e9c">
                           <genre xml:id="genre_76718e1d">article</genre>
                           <genre xml:id="genre_f86b623f">journal</genre>
                           <title level="a" xml:id="title_a895a0ac"/>
                           <title level="j" xml:id="title_9a47c35c"/>
                        </bibl>
                     </biblList>
                     <biblList xml:id="biblList_edac51d2">
                        <head xml:id="head_8e4c8d77">Evidence</head>
                     </biblList>
                  </event>
               </eventList>
               <p xml:id="idm128">The present cantata of which only the printed text has survived was composed before 1761 when it was listed in the Breitkopf catalogue of house manuscripts. This suggests that it originally was performed in Neukirche by Carl Gotthelf Gerlach; Breitkopf later obtained the work from the Gerlach estate in 1761. It was presumably from this catalogue that the cantata was ordered and then performed by the musical society or one of the churches in Zurich in 1770. The present cantata might have been performed on the same occasion as 'Mitten unter den Gedanken' (SchW B2:018 with which the present work is bound), since it clearly has been issued together with this work (continuous page numbers and no title page to the second cantata of the printed text). It should be noted that the text indicates the rather unusual flûtes d'amour (usually tuned a major third or a perfect fourth lower) in the first aria; however, the instruments are not listed in the Breitkopf catalogue of 1761. This is the only work in which Scheibe seems to have employed the flûte d'amour; also Johann Sebastian Bach, Georg Philipp Telemann, Christoph Graupner and Johann Adolph Hasse wrote for the instrument. Besides the instrumentation, the libretto also includes the chorale melodies to be sung by the choir and perhaps also by the audience or congregation.</p>
            </history>
